{"title":"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Eisenstein_Units)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Eisenstein Units)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Third-order_Homogeneous_Linear_Recurrence_Relation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Third-order Homogeneous Linear Recurrence Relation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Polynomial_+_Recursion)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Polynomial + Recursion)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(SO_FAST)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (SO FAST)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(No_Euler&#39;s_Identity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (No Euler's Identity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(1-16)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(1-16)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71cda06e43eecdd7a0e901085820f95d1df0a284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = \\left( \\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right)^n + \\left( \\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"318\" height=\"56\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dac5dec897250384833e3c1b44639bf91cca823a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = \\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf34b5d5793363bab0eff7c657b3b2d91296149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2022)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/30109ee00a294d741de86c20d1ec4fbeb24b6e74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ -1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"411\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Converting both summands to exponential form, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c760c36926a63e2393eabbe1f38e47291a539182.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} -1 + i\\sqrt{3} &amp;= 2e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}}, \\\\ -1 - i\\sqrt{3} &amp;= 2e^{-\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}} = 2e^{\\frac{4\\pi i}{3}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"216\" height=\"49\" />\nNotice that the two terms in the problem are two of the third roots of unity (that is, both of them equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when raised to the power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). \nWhen we replace the summands with their exponential form, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119d918eac02e11217a3156cbae18f23823776ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n) = \\left(e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^n + \\left(e^{\\frac{4\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^n.\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"32\" />\nWhen we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/32603da0074bd25bba0f5d638b0664ab695b67cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2022$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/94919bc4bcb8414ff8ca067e352db7cdcf351cf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2022) = \\left(e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^{2022} + \\left(e^{\\frac{4\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^{2022}.\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"35\" />\nWe can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/251b065c19c721e41102509af48add97a3983246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 674$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, how does that help?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e1052a9fe2051eb77ec32b33115b5551d1a1d2b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2022) = \\left(e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^{3 \\cdot 674} + \\left(e^{\\frac{4\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^{3 \\cdot 674} = \\left(\\left(e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^{3}\\right)^{674} + \\left(\\left(e^{\\frac{4\\pi i}{3}}\\right)^{3}\\right)^{674} = 1^{674} + 1^{674} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\ 2}.\\]\" width=\"695\" height=\"46\" />\nSince any third root of unity must cube to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~ zoomanTV\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Eisenstein_Units.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Eisenstein_Units)\">Solution 2 (Eisenstein Units)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Eisenstein Units)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d4203d19162753092662883ea87292eba67496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/8056535e45f7450deb688aa49c174f606e848a46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"41\" /> are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd79dc1175624e2aa4dd5339573a29840c19b368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Eisenstein Units}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" /> (along with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), denoted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64aa6393454a48fa17402ae3cc648920eb94ebd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, respectively. They have the property that when they are cubed, they equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we can immediately solve:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62dcf0de10dd0f267747770da0f3923528987ca0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\omega^{2022} + \\omega^{2 \\cdot 2022} = \\omega^{3 \\cdot 674} + \\omega^{3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 674} = 1^{674} + 1^{2 \\cdot 674} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\ 2}.\\]\" width=\"452\" height=\"28\" />\n~mathboy100\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Quick_and_Easy)\">Solution 3 (Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by recognizing this form looks similar to the definition of cosine: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c71d8e7450df3420c7b84818aa39449b0b85944.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(x)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}{2}.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"39\" /> We can convert our two terms into exponential form to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d9670d70a67ce52a8b6fed11de123840b74d5c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n) = \\left( e^{\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}} \\right ) ^n + \\left ( e^{-\\frac{2\\pi i}{3}} \\right ) ^n=e^{\\frac{2 \\pi i n}{3}} + e^{-\\frac{2\\pi i n}{3}}.\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"32\" /> This simplifies nicely: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec981a86d201c0a9cf1a40931689eff8d61bcd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)=2\\cos\\left( \\frac{2\\pi n}{3} \\right).\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"43\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df0d9ddf3d37abbe652b35abcb76a89e5df671d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2022)=2\\cos \\left ( \\frac{2\\pi (2022) }{3} \\right) = 2\\cos(1348 \\pi) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2}.\\]\" width=\"428\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~Jackson La Vallee\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Third-order_Homogeneous_Linear_Recurrence_Relation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Third-order_Homogeneous_Linear_Recurrence_Relation)\">Solution 4 (Third-order Homogeneous Linear Recurrence Relation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Third-order Homogeneous Linear Recurrence Relation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice how this looks like the closed form of the Fibonacci sequence except different roots. This is motivation to turn this closed formula into a recurrence relation. The base of the exponents are the roots of the characteristic equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/9220b72df0fad85fb118d975385545820ef9429f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^3-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />. So we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14b8ae055067c69831ec1ac1858e302a8c3ab9b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_0&amp;=2\\\\ a_1&amp;=-1\\\\ a_2&amp;=-1\\\\ a_n&amp;=a_{n-3} \\end{align*}\" width=\"76\" height=\"89\" />\nEvery time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as is true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f32402bff5f1a4ad0287a58b795e42e45339a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2022$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da757320d02b417cf274a9dc2e3e295c1f6378f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n= \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"98\" height=\"30\" />\n~lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Polynomial_.2B_Recursion.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Polynomial_+_Recursion)\">Solution 5 (Polynomial + Recursion)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Polynomial + Recursion)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e380768c4b7f51bd19648ceebd9d07fcd27effb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e0e1ddfc2aeceb68bdaa00ea78d171e30f49ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"43\" />.\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30cbf6c13735c5c7586fb215cf45152155745e85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c65b9569b9881c42a8306635b6cb7d64279d604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\cdot b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />.\nTherefore, a and b are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/61507c5d5fbf5454da22c33cd388f7bbfa5c0b67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + x + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />.\nBy the factor theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc0f1926b0dbe44599de58bbad712f2af5a2027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + a + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a52f61aecf8e0a04b83a4d133f476e7df140f206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 + b + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />.\nMultiply the first equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/23619cb3085fe346fd8d28749fd8c610f8ae786c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{n-2}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> and the second equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf51665a3541f9ac97f2e9bbf47053be7204420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{n-2}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />.\nThis gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/1782c979024601dcdc523b4d56ca884762f7435c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^n + a^{n-1} + a^{n-2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f752716345711713a121bb66c8d1673d743a0950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^n + b^{n-1} + b^{n-2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />.\nAdding both equations together we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b899705e3c91a7c298c9a43dfd6d297b972f0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^n + b^n + a^{n-1} + b^{n-1}+ a^{n-2} + b^{n-2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"321\" height=\"18\" />.\nThis is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d1cbb672dd20dd528c81cc3e5a3f0f3db93f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) + f(n-1) + f(n-2) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"250\" height=\"20\" />.\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9388f4345efa14bc0d632d61bd102fd9d2dea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = -f(n-1) - f(n-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"20\" />.\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc325925d4c412d216b591acfebe72bca3b8009c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,3,4,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e34d2cb80a4cf777e7d3c1791a9546ffc1d6701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = -1, -1, 2, -1, -1, 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore we know that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, our answers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8e0bfad3c13283d333ea3d399fd10b40d529fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E) 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" />.\n~vpeddi18\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28SO_FAST.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(SO_FAST)\">Solution 6 (SO FAST)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (SO FAST)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Converting the two terms into rectangular form, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8e028188a45d19b29dddacde0b94113580e7731.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2022)=\\left(\\cos{\\frac{2\\pi}{3}}+i\\sin{\\frac{2\\pi}{3}}\\right)^{2022}+\\left(\\cos{\\frac{4\\pi}{3}}+i\\sin{\\frac{4\\pi}{3}}\\right)^{2022}.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>By DeMoivre's Theorem, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/34668267a358e8f97461a0f1b45ad200a481481c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2022)=\\left(\\cos{\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\cdot{2022}\\right)}+i\\sin{\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\cdot{2022}\\right)}\\right)+\\left(\\cos{\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\cdot{2022}\\right)}+i\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\cdot{2022}\\right)}\\right).\\]\" width=\"725\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f211b22dd9980f28b4fceb05dd04c4027b8567ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\pi\\cdot{k}}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a897b0025a689c1f6678229dae1d554f7dc795d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{\\pi\\cdot{k}}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>All arguments are even in the second equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf34b5d5793363bab0eff7c657b3b2d91296149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2022)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, so the two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> terms are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> terms are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f56499e74a015d1993c8f7f3533c75a78b7ab912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"126\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28No_Euler.27s_Identity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(No_Euler's_Identity)\">Solution 7 (No Euler's Identity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (No Euler&#39;s Identity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa46fc0525a73384b625940747488cc74b21a3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^{2}=\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f637eab50f6fdd668a462ca4a4ac919752240684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^{2}=\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c66ce79d63c623123226358dfbe6363347044e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^{4}=\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947cb6180cae7d01e85e03088341f32d41f2dc28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^{4}=\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>The binary expansion of 2022 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e740bf3311444e80feee257f5979bbab0d1672.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{10}+2^9+2^8+2^7+2^6+2^5+2^2+2^1\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"17\" /> which can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba832996283505e3ab5410e3097e9f88be90a117.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(4^5+4^4+4^3+4^1)+2(4^4+4^3+4^2+4^0)\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"20\" /> \nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/298bdbc216eda55536d621a02a1109dc3f6d929e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^{2022}=((\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^4)^4\\cdot (((\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^4)^4)^2\\]\" width=\"423\" height=\"41\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d22661360b4799df9282b6be8aeb7e379ce0864e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})(\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2})\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"41\" /> \nSimilarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b013faf80fa3714ed026749af5a99cf47f3d7b73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2})^{2022}=(\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2})(\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"41\" /> \nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2ac05274b4822241f11ab2858a6485335b4e9681.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2022)=2(\\frac{-1+i\\sqrt{3}}{2})(\\frac{-1-i\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 2}\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~ shibepvp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by mop 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ezGvZgBLe8k&amp;t=70s\">https://youtu.be/ezGvZgBLe8k&amp;t=70s</a>\n</p><p>~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Under_2_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Under 2 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ifPUOy_uctM\">https://youtu.be/ifPUOy_uctM</a>\n~<i> Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.281-16.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(1-16)\">Video Solution(1-16)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(1-16)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SCwQ9jUfr0g\">https://youtu.be/SCwQ9jUfr0g</a>\n</p><p>~~Hayabusa1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B\">2022 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017045305\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.071 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 521/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16022/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.618      1 -total\n 60.10%    7.583      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.17%    4.816      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23368:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017045305 and revision id 271623. Re